WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:05.350
I don't know if folks are aware, but we have
to keep covering it.

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:10.459
Corona virus cases have exploded again with
the most cases in the United States in two

00:00:10.459 --> 00:00:11.459
months.

00:00:11.459 --> 00:00:12.790
And new records in 13 states.

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:17.570
Now, I know that the Republican Party and
the Trump administration and the Trump campaign

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:20.560
are acting as if it's over, as if nothing's
going on.

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:25.640
We saw Koven positive Republican Senator Mike
Lee taking his mask off indoors.

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:30.939
Around 80 year olds at yesterday's Amy CONI
Barrat Supreme Court hearings.

00:00:30.939 --> 00:00:32.700
Trump is doing rallies again.

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:35.110
But we do have a pandemic going on and it's
not.

00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:38.220
Going so well, the latest numbers are that
on October 9th.

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:40.690
So that's Friday, I think.

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:46.510
Friday, Saturday, Friday, over the weekend,
we had just shy of sixty one thousand new

00:00:46.510 --> 00:00:47.760
cases in one day.

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:53.530
That's the most new cases in a single day,
dating back almost two months to August 14th.

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:55.880
As you probably know by now.

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:59.030
Deaths lag cases by two to three weeks.

00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:03.510
We've now seen what was a declining death
trend level off.

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:08.120
It's now flat and in all likelihood, it's
already happened twice before.

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:13.320
During this pandemic, when cases spike, deaths
spike two to three weeks later.

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:14.530
That's at the national level.

00:01:14.530 --> 00:01:20.210
Now, there are 13 states, most of them in
the western Midwest, that have new records

00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:23.040
for coronavirus infections over the last week.

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:29.000
These are seven day rolling averages, which
is a better indicator than just a single day.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:35.720
New seven day rolling average highs in Alaska,
Colorado, Indiana, Minnesota, Montana, Nebraska,

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:41.630
New Mexico, North Dakota, Ohio, Oklahoma,
Oregon, South Dakota and Wisconsin.

00:01:41.630 --> 00:01:45.409
The worst of which are in Montana, New Mexico
and South Dakota.

00:01:45.409 --> 00:01:47.960
Now, you might come in and say, oh, but.

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:49.000
But, but, but.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:50.049
But, but, David.

00:01:50.049 --> 00:01:51.049
Clucking like a chicken.

00:01:51.049 --> 00:01:53.670
But what about hospitalizations?

00:01:53.670 --> 00:02:02.720
Well, Indiana, North Dakota, Montana and Nebraska
reporting record high numbers of Corona virus

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:04.090
hospitalizations.

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:06.630
On Sunday, same with Utah.

00:02:06.630 --> 00:02:09.219
So hospitalizations are going up.

00:02:09.219 --> 00:02:14.870
So understand that no matter how many times
Trump says it's disappearing, instead of we've

00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:17.299
turned the corner, he says, we rounded the
turn.

00:02:17.299 --> 00:02:20.060
I understand he's trying to say we turned
the corner.

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:23.180
Thirteen out of 50 states have new record
highs.

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:28.640
That's new peaks in more than a quarter of
American states.

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:31.709
And even in states that aren't at new highs,
numbers are climbing.

00:02:31.709 --> 00:02:36.760
I mean, look, even here in Massachusetts,
for example, we were down to about 150 cases

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:38.349
per day for months.

00:02:38.349 --> 00:02:43.019
We've now once again started to get into the
300 cases per day in September.

00:02:43.019 --> 00:02:46.129
400 cases per day at the end of September.

00:02:46.129 --> 00:02:48.870
Six hundred case days in October so far.

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:52.019
So it is coming back exactly as predicted.

00:02:52.019 --> 00:02:54.139
It's not just flu season.

00:02:54.139 --> 00:02:57.439
We have college students flying around the
country and spreading.

00:02:57.439 --> 00:03:02.260
We have schools, a number of schools having
to very quickly shut things down.

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:07.599
And also that people are exhausted, which
I understand not everybody is being as careful.

00:03:07.599 --> 00:03:10.859
Even people who were being more careful at
a certain point.

00:03:10.859 --> 00:03:14.120
Meanwhile, Trump's back to doing rallies,
if you can believe that.

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:19.790
And we will be talking about that in a little
bit difficult situation because we must vote

00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:21.980
like our lives depend on it.

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:24.749
And yet cases are rising and we want to be
safe.

00:03:24.749 --> 00:03:27.650
We are seeing record lines at early voting.

00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:31.069
We'll have the numbers for early voting on
today's bonus show.

00:03:31.069 --> 00:03:33.159
People mostly wearing masks.

00:03:33.159 --> 00:03:35.000
Orders of magnitude.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:37.999
More early votes this year than in 2016.

00:03:37.999 --> 00:03:39.170
That's great.

00:03:39.170 --> 00:03:40.680
We have to have a plan to vote.

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:43.389
I will be dropping off my absentee ballot.

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:47.389
I think this week in person at City Hall received
it last week.

00:03:47.389 --> 00:03:48.389
I'm ready to go.

00:03:48.389 --> 00:03:54.790
I will film myself dropping it off and post
it as part of my get out the vote effort.

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:55.790
So let us know.

00:03:55.790 --> 00:04:00.790
We'll have a question on our Instagram about
what is your plan for voting.

